Whew.  Finally over. Turns aren't shown (I turned off "time" because I
didn't want to miss the end of any possible "satiated burdened ill"),
but as shown down at the bottom of this post, it took 49290 turns.

Played pettype:none, because pets annoy me and tend to starve me, and I
didn't tame anything throughout the game, hence the petless.  Nethack
should track this for you, IMO.

Did soko before minetown due to lack of poison res.

No particularly remarkable bones piles (did find a minetown bones, but
it didn't have much), no lucky wands of wishing or magic lamps galore
like my last ascension (a Valkyrie, back in February.)  I did get a
fairly early +oID though.  Izchak didn't have enough candles, but the
hardware store made up the difference.

Highlights (or lowlights?) included digging down past Medusa,
forgetting where I was, taking the stairs up, and being stoned.
Thankfully I had an "oLS on, which activated, and I got my towel on in
time.  Medusa disappeared, and so (for some reason) I went downstairs
and took the towel off... didn't take long before I found out where
she'd went.  Down the stairs.  Luckily I'd put on my 2nd "oLS in there
somewhere and that went poof, but this time I killed her for good.

Castle wand was 0:1, so I wished for a magic marker and wrote charging
first try (thankfully!).  Already had boots of speed, so I charged it
and got SDSM and a helm of brilliance.  Later, after finding a ring of
levitation in gehennom (or was it Vlad's?), wished up gauntlets of dex.
 Used a magic lamp found in gehennom for another marker, and wrested
the /oW for +oFoD.  A very, very good decision that I recommend to all
wizards.

Had a bit of trouble in that Asmodeus' lair was right above Juiblex's,
and when I lured Asmodeus down, Juiblex was there to greet me.
Luckily, Asmodeus went down fairly quickly, and I then lured Juiblex up
to dry land, /oDig'd him, and killed him.

Also of note: I couldn't get teleportitis for the life of me after I
had TC.  I finally had to reverse genocide leprechauns -- and of course
got it on the first of those corpses.

The second "incident" that I had was on the top level of Rodney's,
where a gremlin was hanging around the moat.  And wouldn't you know, it
was 10:02 PM server time -- 2 minutes into nighttime.  I lost 9 points
of protection to the durn things as I zapped around before I finally
got the BoTD and levelported down to the VS on level 50.  Invocation
went fine, had a bit of trouble in the sanctum but not too much.
Donated a few more times for protection on the way back up -- was
ticked that I didn't get any at first, so I killed Moloch's priestess
and took my $40k and ran, but kept trying with a priest of Ptah, and
spontaneously got back all 9 points.  As a reward I let Ptah's priest
live.

Didn't have food out on the astral plane, and Famine got me down to
weak before I managed to eat.  This is partially because after FoD-ing
him, I tried to use a wand of teleport to zap other monsters out of the
way -- ressurrecting his corpse.  Repeatedly.  I'm an idiot for not
catching on and just FoDing or /oDing them.

